API-26: give links their initial status and clear demands on load

Until EN_initH, the solver's link status and setting arrays are still
zero from calloc, so EN_STATUS read "closed" for every link and
EN_SETTING read 0 for pumps and valves. EN_DEMAND read the parser's
scratch value: the [JUNCTIONS] demand in user units times the flow
factor, or MISSING for a junction listed in [DEMANDS]. Set each link's
status and setting to its initial ones, and each junction's demand to
0, when the network is loaded. Also document that flows read between
EN_initH and EN_runH are the solver's starting values.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-26_fix.patch

diff --git a/include/epanet2_2.h b/include/epanet2_2.h
index af0dd62..8a340f0 100644
--- a/include/epanet2_2.h
+++ b/include/epanet2_2.h
@@ -316,6 +316,10 @@ typedef struct Project *EN_Project;
   Be sure to call ::EN_initH prior to running a hydraulic analysis using a
   ::EN_runH - ::EN_nextH loop.
 
+  Until ::EN_runH computes the first solution, the flows returned by
+  ::EN_getlinkvalue and ::EN_getnodevalue (such as `EN_FLOW` and
+  `EN_EMITTERFLOW`) are the solver's starting values, not results.
+
   Choose to save hydraulics results if you will be:
   - making a subsequent water quality run,
   - using ::EN_report to generate a report
diff --git a/src/input1.c b/src/input1.c
index bb1db45..d645547 100644
--- a/src/input1.c
+++ b/src/input1.c
@@ -535,6 +535,9 @@ void convertunits(Project *pr)
         {
             demand->Base /= pr->Ucf[DEMAND];
         }
+
+        // The parser used NodeDemand as a marker; no demand is computed yet
+        hyd->NodeDemand[i] = 0.0;
     }
     
     // Convert PDA pressure limits
@@ -630,6 +633,10 @@ void convertunits(Project *pr)
             }
         }
         link->InitSetting = link->Kc;
+
+        // Before a run a link's status and setting are its initial ones
+        hyd->LinkStatus[k] = link->InitStatus;
+        hyd->LinkSetting[k] = link->InitSetting;
     }
 
